#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts: {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Mga kritikal na konsepto: {#critical-concepts}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the measurement of a qubit in a superposition is probabilistic, like "
"flipping a coin, the superposition state itself behaves differently than a "
"flipping coin.\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang ang pagsukat ng isang qubit sa superposition ay probabilistiko, tulad"
" ng paghagis ng barya, ang superposition state mismo ay kumikilos nang "
"naiiba kaysa sa isang baryang lumiligid.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A main difference between a classical probability distribution and a "
"superposition is that the superposition has *phase* coherence, which allows "
"it to interfere constructively or destructively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangunahing pagkakaiba sa pagitan ng isang klasikal na probability "
"distribution at isang superposition ay ang superposition ay may *phase* "
"coherence, na nagbibigay-daan dito na mag-interfere nang constructively o "
"destructively.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The state of a single, isolated qubit can be visualized as a point on the "
"so-called \"Bloch sphere,\" where the relative amplitudes of the "
"$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ components determine the polar angle $\\theta$"
" and the relative phases between the two components determine the azimuthal "
"angle $\\phi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang estado ng isang solong, isolated na qubit ay maaaring ma-visualize "
"bilang isang punto sa tinatawag na \"Bloch sphere,\" kung saan ang mga "
"relatibong amplitude ng mga component na $|0\\rangle$ at $|1\\rangle$ ay "
"nagtatakda ng polar angle na $\\theta$ at ang mga relatibong phase sa "
"pagitan ng dalawang component ay nagtatakda ng azimuthal angle na $\\phi$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All single-qubit quantum gates can be viewed as rotations of the vector on "
"this sphere.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang lahat ng single-qubit quantum gates ay maaaring tingnan bilang mga pag-"
"ikot ng vector sa sphere na ito.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "T/F questions: {#tf-questions}"
msgstr "Mga tanong na T/F: {#tf-questions}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F A quantum superposition is basically the same as a probabilistic event "
"in classical physics, like flipping a coin.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Ang isang quantum superposition ay essentially katulad ng isang "
"probabilistikong kaganapan sa klasikal na pisika, tulad ng paghagis ng "
"barya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F The length of the Bloch vector describing the state of a single isolated"
" qubit is always 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Ang haba ng Bloch vector na naglalarawan sa estado ng isang solong "
"isolated na qubit ay palaging 1.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F Single-qubit quantum gates do not change the length of the Bloch "
"vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"T/F Ang mga single-qubit quantum gates ay hindi nagbabago ng haba ng Bloch "
"vector.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "MC questions: {#mc-questions}"
msgstr "Mga tanong na MC: {#mc-questions}"

